    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d894">

                <pb facs="0967" n="865" xml:id="pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/944: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-08T09:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                                1919, 9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            December 9, 12.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My December 4, 11 a.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d894-f1"/> Julio Acosta elected
                    President of the Republic yesterday by a very great majority. Good order
                    maintained. Saloons closed. Election well conducted. Opposition may have a few
                    deputies owing to proportional method of electing. Particulars by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
